[92mlitellm.completion(model='gemini/gemini-2.5-flash-lite', num_retries=2, drop_params=True, messages=[{'role': 'system', 'content': 'Extract the structured labels from this Crohn\'s disease patient interview. Return only valid JSON matching the schema — no prose, no code fences.\n\nUse the schema\'s enum values exactly. Leave a field null or empty when the transcript does not support a confident value. Set patient_id to the value given in the message.\n\nchurn: set true when the interview looks truncated or the patient disengaged before their story resolved — the narrative is cut off mid-journey, trails off, is very short or vague, or ends with no clear outcome. Set false when the interview reads as a reasonably complete journey. Keep this truncation signal distinct from a topic simply being absent from an otherwise complete story (that is "not mentioned", not churn).\n\ntreatment_records: for each entry, set before_biologic true if the treatment was tried before the patient started or was offered a biologic, and false otherwise.\n\nreferral_pathway: list the patient\'s journey as an ordered sequence of the canonical PathwayStep values.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "patient_id: P000\n\nI'm Alex, 38, male. Diagnosed with Crohn's four years ago. After mesalamine and prednisone failed, my gastroenterologist started me on Humira, which I've taken ever since and it keeps me in remission."}], response_format={'type': 'json_object', 'response_schema': {'$defs': {'ComorbidCondition': {'description': 'Independent coexisting diagnoses only — NOT Crohn\'s-driven sequelae (psoriasis,\nosteoporosis, etc.). Lumping treatment/disease effects in here would make a later "does\ncomorbidity X predict outcome Y" analysis circular. Seeded from P001-P050; extend as found.', 'enum': ['TYPE_2_DIABETES', 'HYPERTENSION', 'HYPERLIPIDEMIA', 'ANXIETY_DISORDER', 'DEPRESSION', 'PCOS', 'ENDOMETRIOSIS', 'MIGRAINE', 'HYPOTHYROIDISM', 'FIBROMYALGIA', 'ASTHMA', 'RHEUMATOID_ARTHRITIS', 'ADHD', 'SLEEP_APNEA', 'OTHER'], 'title': 'ComorbidCondition', 'type': 'string'}, 'Demographics': {'description': 'Self-reported gender/age, grouped so we can later test for demographic differences in\npathways/outcomes. The flat `gender`/`age` spreadsheet columns map into this sub-model.', 'properties': {'gender': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'title': 'Gender'}, 'age': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'title': 'Age'}}, 'title': 'Demographics', 'type': 'object'}, 'PathwayStep': {'description': 'Canonical referral-pathway steps — the draft vocabulary already used to render the\nper-case journey graphs in `data/out/*.html` (mirrors the consolidated phases in\n`src/referral_pathway_analysis.py`). Values are lowercase to match those graph tokens.\n\nMinimal for this iteration: enough to type `referral_pathway` and drive the diagrams. A\ndedicated extraction prompt fills this field; the eventual goal is clustering these per-case\nchains into journey *types* (`docs/SCHEMA.md`). `OTHER` absorbs steps not yet in the vocab.', 'enum': ['symptom_onset', 'self_managed', 'primary_care_contact', 'misdiagnosis', 'diagnostic_delay', 'symptoms_worsen', 'specialist_referral', 'diagnostic_testing', 'crohns_diagnosis', 'conventional_therapy', 'therapy_failed', 'adverse_reaction', 'relapse', 'acute_flare', 'complication', 'surgery', 'comorbidity', 'biologic_recommended', 'patient_fear', 'insurance_denial', 'insurance_appeal', 'insurance_approval', 'insurance_cost_barrier', 'insurance_step_therapy', 'biologic_not_taken', 'biologic_taken', 'biologic_switch', 'loss_of_response', 'remission', 'breakthrough_symptoms', 'alternative_therapy', 'planning_next_step', 'unresolved', 'other'], 'title': 'PathwayStep', 'type': 'string'}, 'ReasonNotTaken': {'description': 'Why a prescribed biologic wasn\'t taken / wasn\'t reached.\n\n`PATIENT_FEARS` lives here (fear of needles/side-effects blocks *taking*, not prescribing);\n`CONTRAINDICATION` and `DEFERRED` were added from real cases (e.g. COPD risk; post-surgery).\n`NOT_APPLICABLE` distinguishes "doesn\'t apply" (biologic was taken) from a blank "not yet\nannotated" cell.', 'enum': ['NOT_MENTIONED', 'EXPLICIT_DENIAL', 'INSURANCE_PROBLEMS', 'COST', 'PATIENT_FEARS', 'CONTRAINDICATION', 'DEFERRED', 'JOURNEY_CUT_OFF', 'UNKNOWN', 'NOT_APPLICABLE', 'OTHER'], 'title': 'ReasonNotTaken', 'type': 'string'}, 'ReasonPrescribed': {'description': 'Why a biologic *was* the chosen path.', 'enum': ['DOCTOR_CHOICE', 'PATIENT_FEARS', 'COST', 'ACCESS', 'NOT_APPLICABLE', 'OTHER'], 'title': 'ReasonPrescribed', 'type': 'string'}, 'TreatmentOutcome': {'description': "Overall outcome. `AMBIGUOUS`/`ONGOING` exist because Crohn's journeys are often circular —\nforcing every patient into SUCCESS/FAILED would fabricate a certainty the transcripts lack.", 'enum': ['SUCCESS', 'FAILED', 'PARTIAL', 'AMBIGUOUS', 'ONGOING', 'UNKNOWN'], 'title': 'TreatmentOutcome', 'type': 'string'}, 'TreatmentRecord': {'description': "One treatment in the patient's history. `before_biologic` marks treatments tried before a\nbiologic was started or considered — the before/after split that answers business Q3 (what is\ntried before a biologic). Set by the model, not inferred downstream, because the biologic may\nnot appear as a treatment at all (e.g. prescribed-but-not-taken).", 'properties': {'name': {'title': 'Name', 'type': 'string'}, 'treatment_class': {'title': 'Treatment Class', 'type': 'string'}, 'outcome': {'$ref': '#/$defs/TreatmentOutcome'}, 'reason_stopped': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'title': 'Reason Stopped'}, 'before_biologic': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'boolean'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'title': 'Before Biologic'}}, 'required': ['name', 'treatment_class', 'outcome'], 'title': 'TreatmentRecord', 'type': 'object'}}, 'description': "One patient's labels — the shared shape of the gold annotations (`.ods`) and a model\nprediction from `extract.py`